PUBLIC RESPONSE: {{1,4},{2,5},{3}}

Chapter 39 is Akashi. In the standard Genji kō no zu the 39th usable pattern is drawn with the five vertical bars 1–5 left to right. The diagram for Akashi shows the first and fourth bars sharing the same mark and the second and fifth bars sharing the same mark, with the third bar standing alone.

That is a two-pair + singleton partition with 1 ≡ 4 and 2 ≡ 5. In set notation with the inner sets written increasingly and the outer list ordered by the minima, this is {{1,4},{2,5},{3}}.

